{"title":"The Theatre Centre:  Far-Flung Peoples  ($20-$30)","startsAt":"2026-11-08T14:00:00-05:00","endsAt":"2026-11-08T15:30:00-05:00","status":"ACTIVE","type":"PHYSICAL","description":"The phone is ringing.\n\nThe roof is banging.\n\nFrench downstairs.\n\nEnglish upstairs.\n\nCaught in the middle: five people, one couch, and a landlord calling it an open-concept bedroom.\n\n**Welcome to Far-Flung Peoples**, an award-winning, fast-paced, multilingual dark comedy set inside a crooked house in downtown Toronto, where its residents are squeezed into a living arrangement that would raise questions at City Hall, if City Hall were paying attention.\n\n*Ticket link is below ($20-$30)*\n\nThe winner of the Norma Epstein Foundation Award and the Hamilton Fringe Best New Canadian Play Contest, *Far-Flung Peoples*, is funny until it is not.\n\nWe'll join our friends at ***Minor Punctuations Theatre*** for this!\n\nhttps://minorpunctuationstheatre.com/our-team/\n\n**TICKET link is here: (you're purchasing for Sunday November 8th @ 2pm)**\n\nhttps://theatrecentre.org/event/far-flung-peoples/\n\nSmall venue space--just 50 seats!! General admission,\n\nWe'll meet in the CAFE before the performance.","venue":{"name":"The Theatre Centre","address":"1115 Queen Street West, Toronto","lat":43.643108,"lng":-79.423256,"city":"Toronto"},"fee":null,"group":"TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE","image":"https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/2/6/a/3/highres_451449891.jpeg"}